        "answer": {
          "short": "$f'(x)=\\dfrac{5x\\sqrt{x}}{2}+\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}f(x)&=\\frac{x^3}{\\sqrt{x}}+\\frac{2x}{\\sqrt{x}}\\\\f(x)&=x^{3-1/2}+2x^{1-1/2}\\\\f(x)&=x^{5/2}+2x^{1/2}\\\\f'(x)&=\\frac52x^{3/2}+x^{-1/2}\\\\f'(x)&=\\frac{5x\\sqrt{x}}2+\\frac1{\\sqrt{x}}\\end{aligned}$$",
